//
// SPRITES.DAT: Sprite data file
//
//
// Name: Sprite name.  Must be under 30 characters.
//
// Base Texture: Texture filename.  For an animated sequence, this is the filename excluding the sequence number.
//				 Both Windows .bmp and Targa .tga file types are supported.  .bmp files must be 24-bit with no
//				 compression, and .tga files must be 32-bit with no compression.  The "base texture" field does not
//				 include the texture's extension.  The engine looks for .bmp files first, and if not found, then
//				 looks for .tga files.
//
// # of Textures: Number of textures in the animation sequence, or 0 if none.  For example, suppose a smoke
//				  animation has 3 textures.  The base texture would be "smoke", the # of textures would be 3,
//				  and the texture filenames would be "smoke0.bmp", "smoke1.bmp", and "smoke2.bmp".
//
// Type:
//		facing	-- always faces viewer
//		upright	-- always faces viewer, but only rotates about y axis
//		xform	-- arbitrary transformation (program controlled -- use for muzzle flashes, light streamers, etc.)
//		(Note: the type doesn't matter for sprites used as decals)
//
// Freq: Animation rate in seconds.  The textures will be cycled at this rate.
//
// Repeat?: 1 to automatically repeat the animated sequence.  0 to play the sequence only once.
//
// Width/Height: Sprite's width and height in inches.
//
// Alpha: The alpha value controls the level of transparency.  1 is fully transparent, and 255 is opaque.  The alpha
//		  value should be set to < 255 when the texture contains an alpha channel (i.e., it's a targa file).
//
// Alpha Mode:
//		normal	-- normal rendering (plants, gates, etc.)
//		add		-- add colors to frame buffer (smoke, sparks, etc.)
//		blend	-- blend colors with frame buffer (decals)
//		corona	-- light corona
//


